# D-STALE-NAME-SETATTR-ADOPTS-PEER-REUSED-INCARNATION-CHANGES-UNRELATED-FILE,
# hypothesis H-SN1: same-build A/B of incarn_poison_unexposed on the reproducer
# tests/stale_name_setattr_reuse.sh, 2/disk/caw/direct on g2b (test15 test16).
# Run from ~/src/mxfs-g: the final-verification build of ~/src/mxfs-f
# (69A9ED8E639EB2D21B613A6) plus the H-SN1 fix and its instrument and nothing
# else (module sources differ from mxfs-f in exactly xfs/xfs_mxfs_reload.c,
# xfs/xfs_inode.h, xfs/xfs_inode.c, xfs/xfs_bmap_util.c, pal/linux/xfs_iops.c).
# 8 iterations a lap, SNR_DELAY_MS 4000 (the harness default), each
# iteration's g<k> new so that it takes f's freed number.
#
# H-SN1: Y's setattr acquire reloads the shell of f's incarnation while the
# platter carries g's; with no descriptor or mapping on the shell the reload
# rebuilds it in place as g, and xfs_setattr_nonsize logs g's core with the
# touch's time.  The instrument P-RELOAD-XINCARN-ADOPT prints at that rebuild
# (every in-place adopt of another incarnation, with the shell's aliases); the
# fix (arm 1) poisons such a shell instead and prints P-RELOAD-XINCARN-POISON.
#
# VERDICT RULES (written before the first lap):
#   SUPPORTED   at least one control lap (arm 0) reads CONTROL-SHOWS-CAUSE
#               (an iteration HIT and Y logged P-RELOAD-XINCARN-ADOPT
#               comm=touch), at least three fix laps (arm 1) read PASS
#               (reused > 0, hit = 0, y_poison_touch > 0, node_failures = 0)
#               with a cold audit CLEAN errors=0, and no fix lap reads FAIL.
#   REFUTED     a control lap HIT whose Y log carries no
#               P-RELOAD-XINCARN-ADOPT comm=touch: the rebuild under the touch
#               is on another path, and its own lines are read before anything
#               else.
#   FIX FAILS   any fix lap FAIL (an iteration HIT, or a node logged a
#               failure), or a fix lap whose cold audit is not CLEAN errors=0:
#               its own lines are attributed first.
#   WEAK        none of the above: more laps, not a verdict.
#   A VACUOUS lap (no iteration reused the number) measured nothing and is
#   rerun; a NOREACH fix lap does not count toward the three; an ABORT or an
#   overrun is read from its own lines.
# The record closes only when this A/B is SUPPORTED and the fix also passes
# the regression laps named on the record.
#
# Bound per lap, from the harness header's step bounds: prep 300 (run.sh's
# prep_cluster row), srcversion, delay and arm read-backs 3 x 20 per node
# (120), mkdir 20, 8 iterations x (20 + 20 + 30 + (4 + 30) + 20), Y's closing
# reset 20, stream copy 120 per node (240), chk_clean 150: 1842 s.
1842 SNR_POISON=0 tests/stale_name_setattr_reuse.sh snr2 8 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
1842 SNR_POISON=1 tests/stale_name_setattr_reuse.sh snr3 8 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
1842 SNR_POISON=1 tests/stale_name_setattr_reuse.sh snr4 8 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
1842 SNR_POISON=0 tests/stale_name_setattr_reuse.sh snr5 8 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
1842 SNR_POISON=1 tests/stale_name_setattr_reuse.sh snr6 8 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
1842 SNR_POISON=1 tests/stale_name_setattr_reuse.sh snr7 8 2/disk/caw/direct g2b
